      ⊣««« ⍝⍝⍝

      Note: Union aka. A ∪ B is neither defined by IBM or by ISO.
       
            Dyalog defines: A ∪ B ←→ A , (B ∼ A) which is somewhat odd and
            asymmetric because duplicate items in A remain duplicated,
            while duplicate items in B are being removed.
       
            GNU takes a more symmetric approach and defines: A ∪ B ←→ ∪ A , B
            which (like a proper mathematical set) removes all dumplicate
            items from A and B.
       »»» ⍝⍝⍝

